-- title:
--   Products over changed points regroup by the profile
-- statement:
--   Fix $s\in\mathbb{N}$. Colors are $0,\dots,s$ and a coloring of a finite set $X$ is a map $a:X\to\{0,\dots,s\}$. For colorings $a,z$ with $z\le a$ pointwise, the changed set is $\{x:z(x)<a(x)\}$, the moved row $i$ is $\{x:z(x)=i<a(x)\}$, and the profile $n_{a,z}(i,h)$ counts points with final color $i<s$ and original color $h>i$. Write $r_i(n)=\sum_hn(i,h)$ and $|n|=\sum_ir_i(n)$. For any $F:\{0,\dots,s\}^2\to\mathbb{R}$,
--   $$
--   \prod_{i<s}\prod_{h}F(i,h)^{\,n_{a,z}(i,h)}=\prod_{x:\ z(x)<a(x)}F\bigl(z(x),a(x)\bigr) .
--   $$
--
--   The likelihood ratio of a move is a product over changed points. It depends on the move only through its profile.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/ExpectationThreshold/ProbabilityLikelihood.lean#L26-L75

